{
  "_source": "The names and the category of every material Woodcore ships (issue #110, spec docs/requirements/active/2026-10-24-onglet-materiaux.md, ARCH-004, ARCH-008). The French names of SIA 261:2020 Tabellen 28 to 30 are read on the French edition, pp. 77-78; their German names are the norm files' own (calc/norms/sia261-2020-tab28/29/30-*.json) and are not repeated here. The workbook's names are the dead-load prototype's translations (docs/requirements/prototypes/2026-10-23-charges-permanentes/lib.py).",
  "_note": "No value lives here: every number is read at its source (calc/norms/, calc/libraries/materials-library.json) -- tests/test_materials_catalogue.py refuses a number in this file. `weights` names, for a material of resistance, the line whose weight a layer of it is weighed with: a member's family, a panel of SIA 265/1 -- a panel without one has no weight, and the tab says so. `includes_battens` names, for a tile of the workbook, the line of SIA 261 Tabelle 29 «… inkl. Lattung» it weighs as (issue #111, P11): the material then carries its battens as the norm's line does -- tests/test_materials_catalogue.py holds the two weights equal.",
